## Mobile and performance requirements

The skill benchmark indicates that mobile can represent more than 75% of ad clicks and reports an 82.9% cross-industry mobile share. These are planning benchmarks, not verified ErgoWorks device data.

### Mobile layout

- Keep the H1, core benefit, CTA and Snapshot limitation visible in the first screen where practical.
- Use a full-width primary CTA.
- Use a sticky CTA only after the visitor scrolls past the hero; it must not obscure content or consent controls.
- Keep tap targets at least **48 × 48 px**, with at least **8 px** spacing.
- Use body text of at least **16 px**.
- Use the correct mobile keyboard for email and phone inputs.
- Keep the phone number clickable with a `tel:` link.
- Avoid horizontal scrolling, carousels and auto-playing audio.
- Do not show an interstitial or popup on arrival.
- Keep form labels visible; do not rely on placeholders as labels.
- Place proof close to the CTA rather than below an excessively long service explanation.
- Ensure the CMP can be dismissed without scrolling and does not cover the CTA.

### Performance acceptance criteria

| Metric | Pass | Warning | Fail |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Largest Contentful Paint | Under 2.5s | 2.5–4.0s | Over 4.0s |
| Interaction to Next Paint | Under 200ms | 200–500ms | Over 500ms |
| Cumulative Layout Shift | Under 0.1 | 0.1–0.25 | Over 0.25 |
| Time to Interactive | Under 3.0s | 3.0–5.0s | Over 5.0s |
| Page weight | Under 2MB | 2–5MB | Over 5MB |

Implementation guidance:

- Use responsive WebP or AVIF hero assets, ideally under 200KB.
- Preload only critical fonts and avoid unnecessary font weights.
- Lazy-load below-fold images.
- Minimise third-party scripts, chat tools and heatmaps.
- Prevent the form, proof strip and consent banner from causing layout shifts.
- QA on representative mobile devices and network conditions before traffic is switched.

These thresholds are build acceptance criteria only, not a sales argument: the existing pages were technically assessed on 2026-07-12 and are fast (live manual-handling page Lighthouse 97 mobile, LCP 2.0s, CLS 0; homepage 98/1.6s). One additional acceptance line applies: **the new LP must match or beat the live page's LCP of 2.0s.** This is a real risk, not a formality — marcuscaporaso.com/ergoworks/campaign-plan scored 92 with LCP 3.3s, so a new LP on a similar stack could be slower than the page it replaces.

