## Testing order and decision rules

Run tests sequentially where traffic is limited:

1. Dedicated message-matched page versus current generic destination. The control is not a slow page: it is a fast (Lighthouse 97), content-heavy but conversion-weak page — single "Make an Enquiry" CTA, full navigation with 30+ links, zero certificate handling and a keyword-stuffed body. Name the specific hypotheses the live page hands us so the test is interpretable rather than "new vs old": **stripped nav vs 30+ nav links; Snapshot offer vs bare enquiry form; certificate block vs none.**
2. Snapshot CTA versus service-specific scope CTA
3. Manual Handling hero copy option
4. Workstation / Assessment hero copy option
5. Hybrid / Home-office hero copy option
6. Proof beside hero CTA versus proof after “How it works”
7. Optional phone field versus no phone field
8. Calendar offered after submission versus consultant follow-up
9. Two-step form versus a shorter single-step control, only after a clean baseline exists

Judge tests on qualified-lead and held-conversation outcomes where sample size permits. Raw form-fill improvements are insufficient if qualification rate deteriorates.

No absolute pause, kill or scale directive should be applied until the target CPA, qualified-lead definition and clean conversion baseline are approved. Any broader 3× kill or 20% scale rule remains conditional on those inputs and sufficient comparable data.

