## Two-step form specification

The form uses progressive disclosure because the complete flow has seven qualification fields plus consent controls. It must optimise for qualified organisational enquiries without collecting sensitive health information.

### Form header

**Request a free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot**

*For one defined organisational workplace question, with a written three-point summary. Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.*

Progress indicator:

- Step 1 of 2 — Your details
- Step 2 of 2 — Workplace need

### Step 1 — Contact

| Field | Type | Requirement | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| First name | Text | Required | Do not request surname unless CRM matching requires it. |
| Work email | Email | Required | Use email keyboard on mobile and inline validation. |
| Company / organisation | Text | Required | Supports B2B qualification. |
| Role | Text or structured select | Required | Options may include WHS/HSE, HR/People, Facilities/Workplace, Operations, Leadership, Procurement, Other. |

**Step CTA:** `Continue to workplace details`

Microcopy:

> Two short steps. Please provide organisational details only—do not include employee injuries, symptoms, diagnoses or medical information.

### Step 2 — Qualification

| Field | Type | Requirement | Options |
|---|---|---|---|
| Team-size band | Single select | Required | 1–25; 26–100; 101–500; 500+ |
| Primary need | Single select | Required | Manual handling training; manual-task review; workstation/office assessment; hybrid/home-office programme; return-to-office/workplace project; ongoing assessment/reporting; not sure yet |
| Timeframe | Single select | Required | Exploring options; within 3 months; 3–6 months; more than 6 months |
| Phone number | Telephone | Optional | Include only if consultant phone follow-up is operationally supported. Use telephone keyboard on mobile. |

Do not include:

- Injury type
- Pain or symptom questions
- Diagnosis or treatment history
- Workers’ compensation status
- Return-to-work medical details
- Employee name or identifiable employee narrative
- “Tell us what happened” or other open-ended medical prompts
- Free-text fields likely to solicit sensitive information

Use a separate governed workflow for any employee-level assessment or return-to-work information.

### Consent controls

These checkboxes must be separate and unticked by default.

**Required service-enquiry acknowledgement**

`[ ] I agree that ErgoWorks may use the details supplied to respond to this enquiry and arrange the requested Snapshot.`

Link “use the details supplied” to the privacy collection notice.

**Optional marketing consent**

`[ ] I would also like to receive workplace-ergonomics insights and service updates from ErgoWorks. I can unsubscribe at any time.`

The enquiry must submit when the marketing checkbox is unticked. Consent records should retain timestamp, notice version and source.

**Submit CTA**

`Request my free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot`

Directly below:

> Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.

### Validation and interaction requirements

- Show inline validation next to the affected field.
- Preserve completed Step 1 fields when Step 2 validation fails.
- Allow users to return to Step 1 without losing data.
- Do not use deceptive preselected answers.
- Do not reject legitimate non-corporate work domains automatically; flag them for qualification instead.
- Store hidden campaign and variant fields without exposing them as user questions.
- Prevent duplicate submissions while the request is processing.
- Provide an accessible success state and confirmation email.
- Do not fire the lead conversion merely because Step 1 was completed.

### Thank-you state

# Your request has been received

ErgoWorks will review the organisational details supplied and confirm whether the question is suitable for the **free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot**.

*The Snapshot provides preliminary guidance and a written three-point summary. It is not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.*

**Primary next step:** optional calendar selection, if consultant capacity and routing support it.

**Secondary next step:** confirmation that ErgoWorks will contact the nominated person.

Do not automatically subscribe the user to marketing. Do not present a newsletter sign-up as the primary post-submission action.

### Lead-quality definition

A landing-page submission becomes a **qualified lead** only after agreed CRM criteria are met. Initial planning criteria:

- Represents an organisation rather than an individual consumer enquiry
- Need falls within ErgoWorks Consulting’s service scope
- Contains sufficient organisational context for follow-up
- Has a plausible delivery timeframe
- Is not intended for ErgoEquip, Biosymm or Physiotherapy
- Is not spam, recruitment, supplier outreach or an unrelated request

Final qualification rules require client approval. The platform event path is `snapshot_request` or `direct_enquiry` → `lead_qualified` → `proposal_sent` → `closed_won`. Snapshot booked and held are CRM stages only, not platform events, and apply only to the Snapshot fulfilment path.

